\section{Conclusion}

This paper frames traffic shockwave forecasting as an evaluation problem rather than an architecture problem. A speed-only STGCN reproduction on PEMS-BAY comes within 0.1\,mph MAE of published reference values, and six months of aligned event and weather records are in place, with descriptive analysis showing a post-game slowdown near SAP Center and a strong seasonal split between wet and dry months. The conditioned model and the window-based evaluation will decide whether exogenous context helps exactly where forecasts earn their keep. \tbd{[we need to replace this with the quantitative answer to both research questions, the main limitation, and one sentence of future work once results exist.]}

